//! SeaORM entity modules for all PAS tables.
//!
//! One entity module per table. Each module exposes:
//! - `Entity` — the entity marker type
//! - `Model` — the read struct
//! - `ActiveModel` — the write struct
//! - `Column`, `Relation`, `PrimaryKey` — generated by `DeriveEntityModel`
//!
//! The v0.44.0 Option C delegation removed `patient`, `practitioner`,
//! `practitioner_role`, and `department` entities — those rows live in
//! `person-service` / `worker-service` and are reached via
//! `crate::upstream` HTTP clients. Dependent tables (encounters,
//! appointments, etc.) reference identity via opaque `person_id` and
//! `worker_id` UUID columns with no DB-level foreign key.

